			"notes": {
				"rationale": "T abbreviates Tausend, as the sentence itself says: the unit the Stückzahl is counted in, Duden's neuter noun das Tausend (Einheit von tausend Stück), not the numeral tausend. So T is a Shorthand member whose Surface is the expansion, not a Variant spelling of the noun and not a Lemma of its own: only a name whose initialism is its usual form keeps its letters as a Lemma (de/abbreviation-is-one-segment). T takes no period. mit makes its Surface Dat.Sg. Like every numeral beyond zwölf, its Reading is 🔢."
